--
--   Description
-- 
-- Tests the events that cause the statistics registers to increment during 
-- gigabit operation in non-burst mode.
-- 
-- Normal Gigabit Operation:
-- 1.  Transmit frame without asserting crs.  This will cause a crs 
--      error to be counted.
-- 2.  Receive a frame one byte below minimum length plus extension 
--      with bad crc. This is a frame fragment and will not affect the 
--      statistics registers.
-- 3.  Receive a frame of minimum length plus extension with bad crc. 
--      This will be counted as a crc error.
-- 4.  Receive a good frame to trigger an interrupt and check statistics.
-- 5.  Receive an undersize frame (smaller than 64 bytes) plus extension 
--      with good crc and then receive a good frame. Check for undersize 
--      frame statistic.
-- 6   Receive an undersized frame (smaller than 64 bytes) plus extension
--      with good crc containing a data code error.
--      Finally receive a good frame and check the statistics.
-- 7.  Receive a jabber (a long frame with bad crc), then a data code error 
--      frame and a carrier extension code error frame.
--      Finally receive a good frame and check the statistics.
-- 8   Receive a carrier extended normal length frame with a symbol error on
--      the first byte of carrier extension.
--      Finally receive a good frame and check the statistics.
-- 9.  Receive a carrier extended minimum length frame with a symbol error 
--      during the data field and carrier extension.
--      Finally receive a good frame and check the statistics.
-- 10. Receive a proper sized frame that is 64 bytes in length plus extension 
--      with the length field indicating 65 bytes. Next, receive a proper sized 
--      frame that is 65 bytes in length plus extension with the length field 
--      indicating 64 bytes. Finally, receive a proper sized frame that 
--      is 64 bytes in length plus extension with the length field indicating 
--      64 bytes.  Check for length field error statistic. Ensure frames with 
--      length field errors are discarded. (Note: Must set bit 16 in the network 
--      configuration register to enable length field detection.) 
-- 11. Receive a minimum sized frame that is 63 bytes long plus extension 
--      with the length field indicating 64 bytes.  (The frame should be 
--      discarded and no length error statistic should set)
-- 12. Receive a minimum sized frame with padding plus extension with a 
--      correct length field. The length field should indicate the length 
--      of the frame to the end of the data field and not include padding.  
--      The frame should be written properly to memory with no length error 
--      statistics set.
-- 13. Receive a frame that is 1518 bytes long with the length field 
--      indicating 1519 bytes. The length of the frame should not be 
--      checked. The frame should be dropped as the actual length
--      is less than the indicated length
-- 14. Receive a maximum sized frame of 1518 bytes with the length field 
--      indicating 1517.  (The frame should be received without a length 
--      error statistic). Check the stats registers
-- 15. Receive a minimum length frame with a id field > 0x600.  The frames
--      length should not be checked and the frame should be received without
--      error.
-- 16. Receive a long frame (1519 bytes) with an indicated length of 1520 bytes.
--      The frame should be dropped due to being too long.  A length error
--      statistic should not be generated.
-- 17. Enable 1536 byte length frames.
--      Receive a frame that is 1536 bytes long with the length field 
--      indicating 1537 bytes.  The actual length is shorter than the
--      indicated length therefore the frame should be dropped
-- 18.  Receive a maximum sized frame of 1536 bytes with the length field 
--      indicating 1535.  (The frame should be received without a length 
--      error statistic)
-- 19. Check the statistics
--
-- This test is used for power consumption evaluation in FIFO mode at 1Gbps

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

